  "body": "Found by the two reviews of PR #4509 (#4341), on head 4f6526650.\n\n## Problem\n\nAfter a tilted section, a setup-change stop (M0/M1) in the Fanuc and Doosan posts lifts Z with `G43.4` still armed. The lift is written by `afterOp` in `assets/posts/fanuc.cps` (about lines 881-887 at 4f6526650). The Go home path and the new tool-change lift of #4341 write `G49` before the lift. This path does not. A reference return (`G28`) while TCPM is active can alarm the control or move the axes in the wrong frame.\n\nMain had the same code before PR #4509. This is not a regression of PR #4509.\n\n## Second question (research)\n\nThe Fanuc and Doosan posts write a bare `G49` before the lift after a tilted section. Find out whether a `G49` that cancels `G43.4` moves Z on these controls. If it does, find a lift that is legal under TCPM.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A setup-change stop after a tilted section writes `G49` before its lift, in the same order as the Go home path.\n- A pinning test in `crates/post/tests/script_rotary/upright_after_tilt/`.\n- The research answer to the second question is recorded in the decision file.\n",
